  "notes": {
    "tone": "Calm, precise, and motion-led. The model should feel like the central character moving through two lives.",
    "pacing": "Use a stable center model and side slots. Training repeats through one active example at a time; error shrinks; the model settles; inference uses the fixed model without feedback.",
    "animation_guidelines": "No comparison slide, no permanent top labels, no giant feedback arrow, no standalone final graph. Generalization should emerge as the trained model opening into a compact pattern panel."
  }
